Moved by Cr MacRae, seconded by Cr Langer

That in accordance with Part 4 of the Town of Cambridge Town Planning Scheme No. 1, Council APPROVES the application for a new two storey dwelling submitted by Artique Building Pty. Ltd. at Lot 1355 (No. 13) Kilkenny Road, Floreat as shown on the plans submitted 23 March 2009, subject to the following conditions:-

(i) the surface finish of boundary walls facing adjacent neighbours being rendered, painted or face brickwork to the satisfaction of the Town;

(ii) any existing crossovers not included as part of the proposed development on the approved plan being closed and the kerb and verge reinstated;

(iii) the retaining wall to the rear and the eastern boundaries being built to a height of RL17.80;

(iv) the crossover being amended to ensure a minimum 1.0 metre setback from the existing verge tree.

Moved by Mayor Mack, seconded by Cr Le Page

That Council:

1. REVOKES Policy 33: Developer Contact with Staff Policy, as contained in Attachment 1;

Moved by Cr Langer, seconded by Cr Pelczar

That the motion be amended to read as follows:- 

That: 

(i) comments received from residents in relation to the proposed installation of lights at the City Beach Tennis Club be noted; 

(ii) the installation of lights at the City Beach Tennis Club be approved subject to the City Beach Tennis Club: 

(a) using the lights only on evenings from Monday to Thursday (inclusive); 

(b) adhering to its Management Plan for the lit courts; 

(c) preparing and undertaking to implement a Management Plan, to be approved by the Administration, to deal with the supervision of children in and around the club facilities on Friday evenings; 

(d) covering that part of the western boundary fence to the tennis courts which is adjacent to the playground and hitting wall with shade cloth or similar material; 

(iii) if the City Beach Tennis Club fails to adhere to either of its Management Plans, the Town may issue a notice under the nuisance prohibition provision of the lease to rectify the situation; and 

(iv) the Town of Cambridge:  

(a) install bollards along the south side of Swanage Avenue to prevent access to the park by cars; 

(b) erect a fence behind the western end of the hitting wall's playing surface; 

(c) decommission the flood lights on the Town's tennis courts in City Beach once the club's lights are in operation.

Moved by Mayor Mack, seconded by Cr Le Page

That Council:

1. REVOKES Policy 33: Developer Contact with Staff Policy, as contained in Attachment 1;

